Status: DONE (technical evidence; human acceptance pending)
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/3
Milestone: Resume progress and carry a backup
Dependencies: 01_PLAYABLE_PROTOTYPE
Purpose: Make the prototype useful beyond one sitting without promising cloud sync.

Tasks:
- [x] Identify games by content, not mutable filenames.
- [x] Persist checkpoints with checked IndexedDB transactions.
- [x] Restore and export/import compatible checkpoints.
- [x] Explain in-game saves, storage failures and browser/origin limitations.

Acceptance criteria:
- Real checkpoint restore survives refresh and matches the same ROM bytes.
- Another ROM cannot accidentally receive a checkpoint.
- Failed writes never produce a success badge.
- Portable backups include identity and runtime compatibility validation.

Completion evidence:
- 2026-11-04: Real core round trip covers manual restore, SRAM capture,
  backup export/import and reload with a renamed ROM.
- Actual 15-second interval and different-ROM rejection exercised.
- Browser transaction abort/quota fixtures retain prior data, show errors and
  leave direct backup export usable. Five unit tests cover helpers/negative input.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-03: Separate battery saves, checkpoints and external backups in design.
- 2026-11-04: Fixed upstream beforeunload core reset corrupting final resume.
  Own checked checkpoint transactions define success, not upstream best effort.
